  {
    "id": "cynbit_blog_002",
    "source": "cynbit.in/blog/rag-architecture",
    "title": "Blog: Building Production RAG Systems",
    "content": "In 'The Architect's Digest', Cynbit published a deep dive on building production-ready RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) systems. The article covers: choosing the right embedding model (dense vs sparse, sentence-transformers vs OpenAI embeddings), vector database selection (FAISS for local, Pinecone/Weaviate for scale), chunking strategies (fixed-size vs semantic chunking), retrieval quality evaluation (recall@k, MRR, NDCG), and anti-hallucination guardrails. The post is based on lessons learned from deploying RAG systems for Cynbit's enterprise clients.",
    "category": "blog",
    "last_updated": "2026-10-29"
  },
  {
    "id": "cynbit_blog_003",
    "source": "cynbit.in/blog/ai-agents-2024",
    "title": "Blog: AI Agent Design Patterns",
    "content": "Cynbit's blog post on AI Agent Design Patterns explores the architectural patterns that underpin reliable autonomous agents: ReAct (Reasoning + Acting), Plan-and-Execute, Reflexion (self-correction), and multi-agent orchestration with supervisor agents. The article discusses when to use single-agent vs multi-agent architectures, how to handle tool call failures and retries, and how to build agents that are transparent and auditable. This post has been referenced by several Indian AI communities and engineering teams.",
    "category": "blog",
    "last_updated": "2026-10-29"
  },
